WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.701
As the students, as

00:00:01.701 --> 00:00:05.105
the young leaders here know, the legacy

00:00:05.472 --> 00:00:08.274
of this extraordinary

00:00:08.274 --> 00:00:11.011
place of education in America

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:13.046
has produced leaders

00:00:13.046 --> 00:00:14.280
who have gone on to be

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:15.715
not only national leaders,

00:00:15.715 --> 00:00:17.617
but global leaders.

00:00:17.617 --> 00:00:19.519
And I'm reminded in particular

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:22.789
this afternoon of two of those leaders,

00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:27.060
the late, great John Lewis,

00:00:31.398 --> 00:00:33.199
and, of course, the phenomenal

00:00:33.199 --> 00:00:35.368
Diane Nash

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:43.743
and what they learned and then taught

00:00:45.045 --> 00:00:46.613
was that

00:00:46.813 --> 00:00:48.848
if one is to understand

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:50.650
that you are born a leader

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:52.018
and it is just a matter

00:00:52.018 --> 00:00:54.120
of when you decide to kick that in,

00:00:55.755 --> 00:00:56.890
then you know

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:58.625
that we will see leadership

00:00:58.625 --> 00:01:00.727
at every stage of life

00:01:00.727 --> 00:01:03.329
if people choose to turn that on.

00:01:04.931 --> 00:01:08.001
And we have seen that here in Tennessee

00:01:09.202 --> 00:01:11.471
over the last couple of weeks.

00:01:12.972 --> 00:01:14.307
We have seen

00:01:15.408 --> 00:01:16.943
over 7000

00:01:16.943 --> 00:01:19.379
students and young leaders

00:01:20.013 --> 00:01:23.850
go to the Capitol to talk about what

00:01:24.184 --> 00:01:25.051
John Lewis

00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:25.985
and Diane Nash

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:28.388
talked about, the importance of freedom,

00:01:29.022 --> 00:01:31.858
the importance of liberty, the importance

00:01:32.592 --> 00:01:35.595
of respecting the right of all people

00:01:35.762 --> 00:01:36.529
to live,

00:01:36.529 --> 00:01:38.164
where they receive dignity,

00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:39.732
where they live in a place

00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:42.001
that they can be free from harm

00:01:44.838 --> 00:01:47.841
And so we are here

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:50.376
understanding the broad shoulders

00:01:51.411 --> 00:01:55.849
upon which we all stand those fighters

00:01:56.683 --> 00:02:00.420
for freedom and liberty and justice.

00:02:01.121 --> 00:02:03.490
Those fighters who understood

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:06.926
the truth must never be stifled

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:08.261
or silenced

00:02:08.261 --> 00:02:11.231
when it is on behalf of the people

00:02:18.805 --> 00:02:20.006
And so I want to start

00:02:20.006 --> 00:02:22.342
by recognizing that Tennessee three

00:02:39.058 --> 00:02:40.093
we are here

00:02:40.093 --> 00:02:42.295
because they and their colleagues,

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:44.964
the Democratic Caucus

00:02:44.964 --> 00:02:46.232
of the state legislature.

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:48.401
And I'd ask you to stand as well, please,

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:01.481
because

00:03:01.948 --> 00:03:04.184
they chose to show courage

00:03:05.752 --> 00:03:09.122
in the face of an extreme tragedy,

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:13.226
which is that 11 days ago,

00:03:14.894 --> 00:03:17.063
six people

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:20.300
three educators

00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:23.937
and three babies, nine years old,

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:26.406
were murdered

00:03:27.173 --> 00:03:28.975
senselessly

00:03:28.975 --> 00:03:31.544
due to gun violence.

00:03:31.878 --> 00:03:33.780
They chose to lead

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:36.149
and show courage to say

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:40.153
that a democracy

00:03:40.153 --> 00:03:42.188
allows

00:03:42.288 --> 00:03:44.657
for places where the people's voice

00:03:44.657 --> 00:03:48.962
will be heard and honored and respected.

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:52.865
And they understood the importance,

00:03:52.865 --> 00:03:57.103
these three, of standing to say

00:03:57.103 --> 00:03:59.272
the people will not be silenced,

00:04:00.206 --> 00:04:02.842
to say that a democracy hears

00:04:02.842 --> 00:04:06.179
the cries, hears the pleas,

00:04:06.679 --> 00:04:10.483
who hears the demands of its people.

00:04:10.717 --> 00:04:12.151
Who say the children

00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:15.288
should be able to live and be safe

00:04:15.288 --> 00:04:18.625
and go to school and not be in fear

00:04:33.606 --> 00:04:35.642
they said,

00:04:35.908 --> 00:04:39.245
We understand when we took an oath

00:04:39.245 --> 00:04:41.948
to represent the people who elected us

00:04:42.548 --> 00:04:43.449
our right,

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:47.520
that we speak on behalf of them.

00:04:49.422 --> 00:04:52.191
It wasn't about the three

00:04:52.191 --> 00:04:53.192
of these leaders.

00:04:53.192 --> 00:04:55.261
It was about who they were representing.

00:04:55.428 --> 00:04:57.063
It's about whose voices

00:04:57.063 --> 00:04:59.699
they were channeling

00:05:00.767 --> 00:05:02.001
Understand that.

00:05:02.001 --> 00:05:05.605
And is that not what a democracy allows

00:05:10.977 --> 00:05:12.011
A democracy

00:05:12.011 --> 00:05:14.380
says you don't silence the people.

00:05:14.447 --> 00:05:16.382
You do not stifle the people.

00:05:16.382 --> 00:05:16.983
You don't

00:05:16.983 --> 00:05:18.584
turn off their microphones

00:05:18.584 --> 00:05:20.920
when they are speaking.

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:23.890
What life and liberty

00:05:28.494 --> 00:05:29.295
that is not

00:05:29.295 --> 00:05:32.432
what or the does

00:05:40.773 --> 00:05:43.543
and understand

00:05:44.444 --> 00:05:47.714
So they turned off the microphones.

00:05:47.714 --> 00:05:49.215
They tried to tell them

00:05:49.215 --> 00:05:52.719
to sit down and be quiet,

00:05:52.719 --> 00:05:55.121
but they understood that the voices

00:05:55.121 --> 00:05:57.957
must be heard. Yes,

00:05:57.957 --> 00:06:00.126
So think about this.

00:06:01.327 --> 00:06:01.994
In order

00:06:01.994 --> 00:06:04.797
to make sure the voices were represented

00:06:05.431 --> 00:06:08.634
in that place where elected leaders

00:06:08.768 --> 00:06:11.404
are supposed to lead in a democracy.

00:06:13.373 --> 00:06:15.241
These leaders have to get a bullhorn

00:06:18.411 --> 00:06:19.379
set to get

00:06:19.379 --> 00:06:21.514
a bullhorn to be heard

00:06:24.417 --> 00:06:25.218
Well, you know what?

00:06:25.218 --> 00:06:29.055
That happens in a democracy, too.

00:06:37.363 --> 00:06:39.599
That happens in a democracy, too.

00:06:39.866 --> 00:06:41.601
If the students demand,

00:06:41.601 --> 00:06:43.035
if the moms demand,

00:06:43.035 --> 00:06:46.572
if the people's demand

00:06:46.939 --> 00:06:48.775
is not being heard

00:06:48.775 --> 00:06:52.378
by those who should listen

00:06:52.378 --> 00:06:53.913
and care.

00:06:53.913 --> 00:06:54.547
Right.

00:06:55.081 --> 00:06:57.283
And contemplate and reflect

00:06:58.217 --> 00:07:00.486
and think about,

00:07:00.486 --> 00:07:02.789
maybe I should give this a moment

00:07:02.789 --> 00:07:04.457
to listen

00:07:06.058 --> 00:07:07.593
give it a fair chance

00:07:07.593 --> 00:07:09.595
to be heard.

00:07:10.963 --> 00:07:13.032
If I feel like I'm so right,

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:14.534
shouldn't

00:07:14.534 --> 00:07:18.271
I have the courage to debate it?

00:07:30.516 --> 00:07:32.218
Make your case.

00:07:32.218 --> 00:07:33.886
Make your case.

00:07:33.886 --> 00:07:36.522
You don't turn off the microphones

00:07:36.522 --> 00:07:37.156
right

00:07:39.525 --> 00:07:41.160
And then

00:07:42.528 --> 00:07:44.063
they do that.

00:07:44.063 --> 00:07:45.031
And then guess what?

00:07:45.031 --> 00:07:46.365
Because you know what?

00:07:46.365 --> 00:07:49.335
Can't have those voices in that room.

00:07:49.669 --> 00:07:51.871
Challenging notions

00:07:51.871 --> 00:07:53.206
about who should say

00:07:53.206 --> 00:07:55.842
what and when and where.

00:07:55.842 --> 00:07:57.510
Oh, let's expel them.

00:07:59.846 --> 00:08:01.981
Can you imagine?

00:08:01.981 --> 00:08:04.417
Let's get rid of them entirely.

00:08:05.651 --> 00:08:07.253
Let's remove them.

00:08:07.253 --> 00:08:09.255
Not only for that moment.

00:08:10.790 --> 00:08:11.891
But remove

00:08:11.891 --> 00:08:14.560
these people who have been elected

00:08:15.061 --> 00:08:17.196
to represent the people

00:08:18.831 --> 00:08:21.067
and let us decide

00:08:21.067 --> 00:08:24.737
who should represent the people

00:08:26.739 --> 00:08:27.473
What is that?

00:08:27.473 --> 00:08:30.209
That is not a democracy.

00:08:30.209 --> 00:08:32.311
That is not a democracy.

00:08:32.311 --> 00:08:35.781
You can't walk around with your lapel pin

00:08:46.192 --> 00:08:48.461
and you're not representing the values

00:08:48.461 --> 00:08:50.463
that we hold dear as Americans.

00:08:52.832 --> 00:08:54.534
You can't walk around and talk

00:08:54.534 --> 00:08:55.835
about protocol.

00:08:55.835 --> 00:08:59.939
Protocol and procedures were devised

00:09:00.006 --> 00:09:01.140
to require

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:03.209
and allow and encourage

00:09:03.209 --> 00:09:05.011
debate and discussion.

00:09:05.011 --> 00:09:08.014
And, yes, dissension

00:09:14.353 --> 00:09:15.855
Let these so-called leaders

00:09:15.855 --> 00:09:19.592
try to shut it down instead

00:09:19.892 --> 00:09:22.028
But we're not having that

00:09:23.362 --> 00:09:25.631
We're not having that.

00:09:25.731 --> 00:09:29.702
And so the thousands of young leaders

00:09:30.303 --> 00:09:33.339
who descended on the Capitol and continue

00:09:33.339 --> 00:09:34.574
to organize,

00:09:36.075 --> 00:09:38.044
continue to require

00:09:38.044 --> 00:09:40.580
that the voices be heard

00:09:42.214 --> 00:09:43.883
because let's understand,

00:09:43.883 --> 00:09:46.886
the underlying issue

00:09:46.886 --> 00:09:48.554
is about fighting

00:09:48.554 --> 00:09:51.857
for the safety of our children.

00:10:01.767 --> 00:10:03.402
Saying that,

00:10:03.402 --> 00:10:06.505
you know, our babies are going to school.

00:10:06.539 --> 00:10:08.741
It's been years now where they're taught

00:10:09.475 --> 00:10:12.178
to read and write and hide in a closet

00:10:12.178 --> 00:10:13.346
and be quiet.

00:10:13.346 --> 00:10:13.846
If there is

00:10:13.846 --> 00:10:17.550
a mass shooter at their school,

00:10:18.117 --> 00:10:19.752
where our children

00:10:19.752 --> 00:10:20.886
who have

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:23.990
God's capacity to learn and lead,

00:10:24.223 --> 00:10:26.959
who go to school in fear

00:10:27.593 --> 00:10:30.830
if their back is to the back of the door,

00:10:32.698 --> 00:10:34.333
that they don't know what might be coming

00:10:34.333 --> 00:10:36.502
through the door,

00:10:37.503 --> 00:10:40.172
Our children are being traumatized

00:10:40.573 --> 00:10:42.908
right now by this fear.

00:10:44.043 --> 00:10:46.612
Parents are wondering and asking

00:10:47.413 --> 00:10:49.649
and praying

00:10:49.982 --> 00:10:50.783
every time

00:10:50.783 --> 00:10:52.585
they send their child to school

00:10:52.585 --> 00:10:54.320
or take their child to school, that

00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:56.355
their baby might come home safe.

00:10:58.824 --> 00:10:59.492
Think about the

00:10:59.492 --> 00:11:02.561
underlying issue

00:11:04.096 --> 00:11:04.363
You know,

00:11:04.363 --> 00:11:06.832
some things are up for partizan debate.

00:11:08.134 --> 00:11:09.168
Sure.

00:11:10.169 --> 00:11:10.903
And they will be

00:11:10.903 --> 00:11:11.771
because that is also

00:11:11.771 --> 00:11:13.873
a sign of a democracy.

00:11:13.873 --> 00:11:16.942
But on the issue of smart gun

00:11:16.942 --> 00:11:19.645
safety laws,

00:11:19.945 --> 00:11:22.615
background checks of all

00:11:22.615 --> 00:11:24.517
background checks,

00:11:30.756 --> 00:11:32.091
the policy is really

00:11:32.091 --> 00:11:34.293
pretty straightforward.

00:11:34.527 --> 00:11:36.295
It's to say

00:11:36.295 --> 00:11:39.165
you might want to know

00:11:39.799 --> 00:11:42.001
before someone buys a gun,

00:11:42.702 --> 00:11:44.070
whether they've been found

00:11:44.070 --> 00:11:46.172
by a court to be a danger to themselves

00:11:46.172 --> 00:11:46.605
or others.

00:11:46.605 --> 00:11:49.008
You just might want to know

00:11:51.043 --> 00:11:53.512
you might want to know

00:11:53.512 --> 00:11:56.115
if someone has shown themselves

00:11:56.115 --> 00:11:56.816
to be violent

00:11:56.816 --> 00:11:58.651
before they can go and buy a gun.

00:11:58.651 --> 00:12:00.686
You just might want to know

00:12:01.954 --> 00:12:03.723
it's reasonable.

00:12:03.723 --> 00:12:05.925
The mayor talked about red flag laws

00:12:07.359 --> 00:12:08.861
when we know

00:12:08.861 --> 00:12:11.430
and when a community or a family knows.

00:12:12.631 --> 00:12:14.133
Shouldn't we listen?

00:12:14.133 --> 00:12:15.735
All right.

00:12:15.735 --> 00:12:18.571
Shouldn't we listen to assault

00:12:18.571 --> 00:12:21.307
weapons or

00:12:23.275 --> 00:12:25.711
these are weapons of war, right?

00:12:27.480 --> 00:12:30.382
These are weapons that were designed

00:12:31.083 --> 00:12:33.352
to kill a lot of people.

00:12:33.519 --> 00:12:34.954
Quickly,

00:12:36.322 --> 00:12:38.424
no place on the streets

00:12:38.424 --> 00:12:41.293
of the civil society

00:12:52.538 --> 00:12:55.341
Part of the underlying point

00:12:55.341 --> 00:12:57.409
is let's not fall

00:12:57.443 --> 00:13:00.813
for the false choice.

00:13:00.813 --> 00:13:03.182
We suggest you're either in favor

00:13:03.182 --> 00:13:04.950
of the Second Amendment

00:13:04.950 --> 00:13:07.153
or you want reasonable gun safety.

00:13:07.153 --> 00:13:07.853
Laws.

00:13:07.853 --> 00:13:09.855
We can and should do both.

00:13:15.961 --> 00:13:16.662
Don't fall

00:13:16.662 --> 00:13:19.365
for the false choice

00:13:20.399 --> 00:13:24.036
So the underlying issue

00:13:24.136 --> 00:13:25.805
is one

00:13:26.071 --> 00:13:28.808
that we are witnessing over

00:13:28.808 --> 00:13:30.109
and over again.

00:13:30.109 --> 00:13:32.211
This community

00:13:32.311 --> 00:13:34.547
experienced it firsthand.

00:13:35.681 --> 00:13:38.551
Just 11 days ago,

00:13:38.551 --> 00:13:41.821
I have been to Atlanta,

00:13:42.855 --> 00:13:45.090
I have been to Buffalo,

00:13:46.192 --> 00:13:49.094
I have been to Highland Park

00:13:49.094 --> 00:13:51.263
and Monterey Park

00:13:51.263 --> 00:13:54.300
just in the last several months.

00:13:57.603 --> 00:13:58.537
You know, and

00:13:58.537 --> 00:13:58.838
and the

00:13:58.838 --> 00:13:59.438
thing is, is

00:13:59.438 --> 00:14:01.574
that it's not like we're trying

00:14:01.574 --> 00:14:02.741
to figure out

00:14:02.741 --> 00:14:06.045
how we should deal with a policy

00:14:06.045 --> 00:14:08.848
around smart gun safety laws.

00:14:09.081 --> 00:14:11.584
The ideas are there.

00:14:11.584 --> 00:14:14.053
The issue which gets back to

00:14:14.053 --> 00:14:15.988
these three

00:14:17.723 --> 00:14:19.124
is that

00:14:19.124 --> 00:14:22.228
we need leaders who have the courage

00:14:22.895 --> 00:14:24.997
to act

00:14:27.166 --> 00:14:28.934
at statehouses

00:14:28.934 --> 00:14:30.636
and in Washington, D.C.,

00:14:30.636 --> 00:14:34.173
in the United States Congress,

00:14:35.007 --> 00:14:37.676
have the courage to act

00:14:47.386 --> 00:14:49.488
instead of the cowardice,

00:14:49.955 --> 00:14:53.425
to not allow debate and to not allow

00:14:53.425 --> 00:14:55.661
a discussion on the marriage piece

00:14:56.595 --> 00:15:00.032
of what is at stake

00:15:01.166 --> 00:15:02.401
courage.

00:15:02.401 --> 00:15:03.335
All right.

00:15:04.036 --> 00:15:06.105
You can't call yourself a leader

00:15:07.239 --> 00:15:10.142
if you don't have the courage to know

00:15:10.309 --> 00:15:11.277
what is right

00:15:11.277 --> 00:15:12.544
and act on it,

00:15:12.544 --> 00:15:14.546
regardless of the popularity

00:15:14.546 --> 00:15:16.382
of the moment.

00:15:31.931 --> 00:15:33.832
So I'm going to close with this point

00:15:35.901 --> 00:15:38.504
I do believe

00:15:38.504 --> 00:15:42.574
that every generation has its calling

00:15:43.709 --> 00:15:44.476
and

00:15:47.846 --> 00:15:50.249
that there are moments in time

00:15:50.816 --> 00:15:53.752
that find you

00:15:53.852 --> 00:15:55.154
and require

00:15:55.154 --> 00:15:58.724
and depend on your leadership.

00:15:58.724 --> 00:16:00.092
And so in particular,

00:16:00.092 --> 00:16:03.028
to all the young leaders here,

00:16:05.397 --> 00:16:06.765
this issue

00:16:06.765 --> 00:16:09.068
is going to require your leadership.

00:16:10.569 --> 00:16:12.071
It is

00:16:13.372 --> 00:16:14.907
I spent time

00:16:14.907 --> 00:16:15.874
as the United States

00:16:15.874 --> 00:16:17.142
Senate senator

00:16:17.142 --> 00:16:19.345
in the United States Congress.

00:16:19.345 --> 00:16:21.280
Before that, I was an attorney general

00:16:21.280 --> 00:16:22.181
leading the second

00:16:22.181 --> 00:16:23.415
largest department of Justice

00:16:23.415 --> 00:16:25.451
in the United States.

00:16:26.285 --> 00:16:28.053
I'm now vice president of United States.

00:16:28.053 --> 00:16:30.289
And I'm telling you

00:16:35.394 --> 00:16:37.663
and I'm sharing that with you.

00:16:38.430 --> 00:16:40.766
I'm sharing that with you.

00:16:40.766 --> 00:16:43.002
The young leaders here

00:16:43.002 --> 00:16:45.437
to tell you, we need you.

00:16:46.672 --> 00:16:48.607
We need you

00:16:48.607 --> 00:16:52.277
every moment every movement

00:16:52.678 --> 00:16:54.880
in my perspective

00:16:54.880 --> 00:16:56.448
that has been about progress

00:16:56.448 --> 00:16:57.483
in our country

00:16:58.417 --> 00:16:59.251
was led

00:16:59.251 --> 00:16:59.685
by the

00:16:59.685 --> 00:17:00.753
young leaders

00:17:00.753 --> 00:17:03.355
like John Lewis and Diane Nash.

00:17:03.489 --> 00:17:04.923
And you

00:17:07.860 --> 00:17:08.160
in

00:17:11.663 --> 00:17:13.699
every one of our

00:17:15.367 --> 00:17:17.503
And so we are going to be

00:17:18.303 --> 00:17:21.340
depending on you

00:17:21.340 --> 00:17:23.142
in solidarity with the work

00:17:23.142 --> 00:17:24.810
we will all do.

00:17:24.810 --> 00:17:28.781
In our respective positions

00:17:28.981 --> 00:17:30.783
to lead.

00:17:31.650 --> 00:17:34.153
You speak with such clarity

00:17:34.420 --> 00:17:37.689
and you speak

00:17:37.689 --> 00:17:39.725
by telling the truth

00:17:39.725 --> 00:17:41.994
through a lived experience.

00:17:42.995 --> 00:17:45.764
Your voices

00:17:45.764 --> 00:17:47.399
are part of the conscience

00:17:47.399 --> 00:17:49.735
of our country.

00:17:51.170 --> 00:17:53.238
When we need in these moments

00:17:53.238 --> 00:17:54.573
in time,

00:17:54.573 --> 00:17:56.975
people who have something in them

00:17:57.476 --> 00:18:00.946
that is about empathy,

00:18:01.747 --> 00:18:04.650
about care

00:18:05.751 --> 00:18:08.587
about a sense of responsibility

00:18:09.021 --> 00:18:12.324
for their brother and sister

00:18:12.925 --> 00:18:14.827
we need you all

00:18:16.762 --> 00:18:19.565
and your leadership in this movement

00:18:20.999 --> 00:18:23.735
is going to impact people

00:18:23.735 --> 00:18:26.271
that you may never meet.

00:18:26.305 --> 00:18:29.341
People who may never know your name,

00:18:29.341 --> 00:18:31.510
but because of your leadership,

00:18:32.244 --> 00:18:34.146
they will forever be benefited

00:18:35.581 --> 00:18:38.383
So I say all that to say

00:18:38.383 --> 00:18:40.853
we will not be defeated yet.

00:18:41.353 --> 00:18:43.522
We will not be deterred

00:18:44.790 --> 00:18:47.192
We will not throw up our hands

00:18:47.192 --> 00:18:50.762
when it is time to roll up our sleeves.

00:18:51.096 --> 00:18:52.564
We will fight.

00:18:52.564 --> 00:18:54.066
We will lead.

00:18:54.066 --> 00:18:56.101
We will speak with truth.

00:18:56.435 --> 00:18:59.938
We will speak about freedom and justice.

00:19:03.008 --> 00:19:04.710
And we will march on.

